# Two survivors inside a spin hint, for the same reason as most of ring_poll's.
#
#     for _ in 0..=( attempt % 8 )
#     {
#       core::hint::spin_loop();
#     }
#     true
#
# The loop bound decides how many hint instructions execute and nothing else —
# the arm returns the constant `true` either way. `% 8` becoming `+ 8` or `/ 8`
# changes the iteration count and no observable value, so no assertion can
# separate them.
#
# Worth being clear about what is *not* being excused here: `pause`'s return
# value is tested, at both polarities, in this crate's own suite. What survives
# is only the backoff shape, which is a performance property. Asserting it would
# mean asserting on a clock — the same trade `ring_bench` refuses and for the
# same reason.

ring/ring_wait/src/lib.rs:121:30: replace % with + in pause
ring/ring_wait/src/lib.rs:121:30: replace % with / in pause
